    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 telephone for humans, keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nThree small, cohesive touches:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` property to the `OwnerDto` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec), matching the existing derived-field pattern.\n\n2. **`TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a small self-contained helper following the existing `CityLocality`/`CheckDigit`/`HouseholdId` convention: splits the E.164 number into country code (longest known 1\u20133 digit calling code, defaulting to two digits for the app's `+61`) and national digits grouped in threes, e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Non-E.164 input is returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: the only existing function changed is the abstract `toOwnerDto` mapping (one added annotation line, CC 1), and all new behaviour lives in a new class with essentially no surrounding complexity. The acceptance test (and the full suite) pass.",
